From: Lars <118484383+LarzVader@users.noreply.github.com>
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: aic: load the BSP firmware without a device

The BSP downloads the firmware through SDIO function 1 before the WLAN
driver binds that function. request_firmware() with that device adds a
firmware-cache devres entry (fw_add_devm_name) to the still unbound
function, so the WLAN probe fails with -EBUSY ("Resources present before
probing") and no interface appears. The data is copied into a private
buffer and released right away, so request it without a device.

---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/aic/aic8800_bsp/aic_bsp_driver.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/aic/aic8800_bsp/aic_bsp_driver.c
@@ -491,7 +491,14 @@
 	if (!fw_name)
 		return -ENOMEM;
 
-	ret = request_firmware(fw, fw_name, dev);
+	/*
+	 * dev is SDIO function 1, which the BSP drives without being bound to
+	 * it; the WLAN driver binds it afterwards. request_firmware() would add
+	 * a firmware-cache devres entry to it, and that probe then fails with
+	 * -EBUSY ("Resources present before probing"). The data is copied and
+	 * released right away, so load it without a device.
+	 */
+	ret = request_firmware(fw, fw_name, NULL);
 	kfree(fw_name);
 
 	return ret;
